          "title": "You'll want to know: überziehen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "überziehen — \"to overdraw (an account); to overrun\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Er hat sein Konto um zweihundert Euro überzogen. He has overdrawn his account by two hundred euros."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In this sense inseparable: er überzieht, er hat überzogen. Separable when you pull something on over: Er zieht eine Jacke über."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "überziehen is built from über \"over\" and ziehen \"to pull, to draw\", inherited from Old High German ziohan and Proto-Germanic teuhaną (EtymDB): you draw out more than is there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
